# Regenerable program output. CLAUDE.md states outright that tests/<set>/merged.png
# and tests/<set>/debug/ are safe to delete at any time. Together they are ~995 MB
# against the corpus's 73 MB of actual screenshots, so ignoring them is the
# difference between a ~100 MB repo and a 1.1 GB one.
#
# The *input* screenshots under tests/ are deliberately NOT ignored. They are the
# regression corpus: tools/baseline.py runs all 24 sets, and the ground-truth
# tables in CLAUDE.md key to those exact files. Note they carry player handles in
# the HUD -- badland_test3/cym.png reads "Waiting for yodagem..." across its top
# band -- which is why this repo is private. Redacting them is not the
# alternative: those pixels are documented program behaviour (see the --top-crop
# residual note in CLAUDE.md's deferred section) and editing them would silently
# invalidate the baselines.
debug/
merged.png

# tools/baseline.py's stored run, captured on demand with -o. Regenerable, and a
# stale one sitting in the tree invites comparing against the wrong baseline.
before.json

# 194 MB, and rebuilds from requirements.txt, which is pinned.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The Discord token. polybot reads DISCORD_TOKEN from the environment and
# compose.yaml resolves ${DISCORD_TOKEN:?} from a .env beside it. Never commit it.
.env

# Editor and tool state, per-user rather than per-project. PyCharm keeps this
# project's per-test-set run configurations in .idea/workspace.xml, which
# JetBrains' own .idea/.gitignore already treats as local state.
.idea/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Superseded, kept locally as a reference. Nothing imports it and the Dockerfile
# does not copy it.
polymerge_old.py
